<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Grahovac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1858</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Grahovo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Grahovac was fought in May 1858 at Grahovac in western Montenegro, where Montenegrin forces under Grand Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirko-petrovic-njegos">Mirko Petrović-Njegoš</a> defeated an Ottoman army. The victory brought diplomatic intervention by the great powers, whose commission drew the first internationally recognised border of Montenegro in 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-grahovac.jpg" alt="Battle of Grahovac" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grahovobattle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
